-- Lem417.seg: what each declaration's informal text opens.
-- Notation (opened to expose the shape of a type, "A x", a pair, Id Bool _ true):
--   Cl Iff Cap Sub Eqv tau M scA OTc Tr Tr3 LT EQ TT OK NZ InC Lex Cs C4 Y5 X5 Down PsiP
--   NFsum NFsum' NFphi NFom, Clos's packages (DC DSum DCard DR WD WDp WDo WU WUs WUp WUo WU0 H415
--   Bnd), and this file's packages and their parts (H17 SumMid MidP SM SumQ PhiQ PhiP PhiS OmP
--   OmS KmF PC CP CS Star).  A package is opened where it is built (wp-step, w-om, claim,
--   rem417c) and by its accessors.
-- C (the class C^a(A)) is opened in the (*) steps st-plus, st-phi, st-om, st-loI: "u in C^a(A)"
--   gives "u in OT" (ca-ok), the first component.
-- Definitions opened where the text says "by definition":
--   cat ((g, c) = cat g c, (b0, bs) c = (b0, cat bs c)) in mid-plus, sm-plus, sum-mid;
--   isA, isG, isZero (an atom; 0) in the clause-by-clause splits sm-atom, sm-plus, sum-mid, wp-rec;
--   le (u <=' b is u <' b or u = b) in le-antisym, le-of-lex;  kminus in km-om, til-km;
--   tilde, card, cardS (Def. 2.13(b)) in til-nfom, tilde-ii, til-psiR, til-psiI, card-le (tilde x = (card x).1);
--   SP (s + 1 = e) in km-F, til-km;  Mc (card-M) in card-le;
--   inC, isOT, isR, and (Defs. 2.8(b), 2.9) in own-inC, ok-psi;  allLt in allLt-cons.
-- allLt-cons (refl) also opens and/lt/fwd/cmp2: unfolding allLt at (h, M) and then "and"
-- evaluates lt h y (a checker artefact, as Clos.card-phi); its use in not-own opens none of them.
